# MUAY THAI

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Muay Thai.

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the specific performance profile of Muay Thai athletes and individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Muay Thai is a striking combat sport characterized by the integrated use of punches, kicks, knees, elbows and clinch fighting.

Success depends on the athlete's ability to:

Strike efficiently.

Control distance.

Dominate the clinch.

Maintain balance under contact.

Adapt continuously throughout the fight.

---

# Philosophy

Muay Thai is often called "The Art of Eight Limbs."

Unlike most striking sports, it combines long-range striking with prolonged close-range exchanges.

The athlete must generate force while remaining stable under constant physical contact.

Power, timing, balance and resilience are equally important.

